/* The header for this test is at the BOTTOM of this file, below the script.
   It is there because a constant inside a leading comment can swallow the
   rest of the file in the engine - see RMSTEST_56 and the directory README.
   Nothing below the script can do any harm. */

<PLAYER_SETUP>
  random_placement

<LAND_GENERATION>
  base_terrain GRASS

<ELEVATION_GENERATION>


<TERRAIN_GENERATION>


<OBJECTS_GENERATION>

  /* FLOOR_BEFORE - unconditional, outside every random block. Sanity that the
     file parsed and ran at all. */
  create_object WILD_BOAR
  {
    number_of_objects 25
    set_gaia_object_only
  }

  /* OUTER start_random. Pinned 100/0, so branch 1 is the only one that can
     legitimately fire under correct semantics. */
  start_random
    percent_chance 100

      /* OUTER_CHOSEN_HEAD - proves the engine entered branch 1's body. */
      create_object GOLD
      {
        number_of_objects 20
        set_gaia_object_only
      }

      /* INNER start_random, nested inside the outer's chosen branch. Also
         pinned 100/0. */
      start_random
        percent_chance 100
          /* INNER_CHOSEN */
          create_object CYPRESS_TREE
          {
            number_of_objects 20
            set_gaia_object_only
          }
        percent_chance 0
          /* INNER_UNCHOSEN - must not appear under correct inner selection. */
          create_object OLIVE_TREE
          {
            number_of_objects 20
            set_gaia_object_only
          }
      end_random

      /* AFTER_INNER - still inside the outer's chosen branch, after the
         inner block's own end_random. */
      create_object BIRCH_TREE
      {
        number_of_objects 20
        set_gaia_object_only
      }

    percent_chance 0
      /* OUTER_UNCHOSEN - THE decisive marker. Must not appear if the outer's
         branch exclusivity survives the inner block intact. */
      create_object STONE
      {
        number_of_objects 20
        set_gaia_object_only
      }
  end_random

  /* TAIL_AFTER - unconditional, after the outer's own end_random. */
  create_object ASIAN_PINE_TREE
  {
    number_of_objects 20
    set_gaia_object_only
  }

<CONNECTION_GENERATION>


/*
================================================================================
RMSTEST_68 - nested start_random: what does the inner end_random actually
close
docs/known-issues.md BUG-020, src/parser/parser.ts (RMS0213),
docs/parser-design.md verify item 20, de-official-map-issues.md Sec.6
(includes/F_seasons.inc, ten nested sites reached by 43 shipped scripts)
================================================================================

THE QUESTION
F_seasons.inc nests a start_random inside another start_random at ten sites.
Our parser detects the nesting structurally and emits RMS0213 (lossless - the
AST keeps the nested block rather than discarding it), but parser-design's own
verify item 20 already records the actual engine resolution as UNMEASURED. The
suspicion, inferred only from the guide's prohibition on nesting rather than
from an observation: the inner end_random closes the OUTER start_random
instead of the inner one, so the inner block's own terminator never really
exists as far as the engine's random-selection state is concerned, and
whatever comes after it - including the OUTER's remaining, supposedly-
unselected branches - runs unconditionally.

METHOD
Every percent_chance in both blocks is pinned to 100/0, so which branch a
CORRECTLY nested pair of start_random blocks would pick is known in advance
with no run-to-run variance. Six markers are placed at the six positions where
the hypothesis and the correct-nesting reading disagree or agree, plus a floor
control before everything and a tail control after everything, so a
completely broken/blank generation is distinguishable from a working one that
simply answers the question. One command per marker, one object type per
marker, so the read is a headcount only - no position math needed.

READ-OFF TABLE
  WILD_BOAR (floor, before anything)        expect 20-25   file parsed and ran;
                                             if this is 0, nothing below is
                                             readable - regenerate and check
                                             for an unrelated script error
                                             first
  GOLD (outer branch 1's head)              expect ~20     outer picked its
                                             100% branch, as it must under
                                             either reading - if this is 0,
                                             something is wrong with pinned
                                             percent_chance itself and this
                                             run cannot be trusted (see
                                             RMSTEST_55, which already
                                             confirmed pinned percent_chance
                                             works for a NON-nested block)
  CYPRESS_TREE (inner branch 1)             expect ~20     inner picked its
                                             100% branch
  OLIVE_TREE (inner branch 0)               expect 0       inner branch
                                             exclusivity intact
  BIRCH_TREE (outer branch 1, after the
              inner block's own end_random) expect ~20     outer branch 1's
                                             body continues normally past the
                                             nested block
  STONE (outer branch 0)                    expect 0 IF nesting resolves
                                             correctly; NONZERO is the
                                             suspected defect CONFIRMED - the
                                             inner end_random consumed the
                                             outer's random state early, and
                                             everything from outer branch 0
                                             onward ran unconditionally
  ASIAN_PINE_TREE (tail, after the outer's
                   own end_random)          expect ~20     if this reads 0
                                             while everything above the STONE
                                             row looks normal, the outer's
                                             real end_random - now with no
                                             random state left to close under
                                             the corruption hypothesis -
                                             became a dangling token that
                                             broke something downstream rather
                                             than being silently ignored;
                                             record this as its own finding
                                             even though the STONE row already
                                             answered the main question

READING THE COMBINATION
  STONE=0, OLIVE_TREE=0, everything else present    nesting resolves exactly
    as lexically written. The suspected defect is REFUTED for this two-level
    case. RMS0213's message can state the consequence ("resolves correctly,
    but the engine does not support this - avoid it for portability") instead
    of only the prohibition, per this bug's own prescribed fix.
  STONE>0                                            THE hypothesis, confirmed.
    RMS0213 needs to say so explicitly, and instantiate.ts's random-block
    handling needs the same correction wherever it currently assumes a
    start_random's own end_random terminates only itself.
  OLIVE_TREE>0, STONE=0                              a different defect: inner
    branch selection is broken (e.g. reading a shared roll instead of its own)
    while outer exclusivity survives. Worth its own RMSTEST rather than being
    folded into this one's conclusion.
  BIRCH_TREE=0 with STONE=0                          the inner block silently
    swallows the REST of the outer's chosen branch too, not just the outer's
    unchosen one - a third shape, and grounds to re-read F_seasons.inc's ten
    sites specifically for whether anything follows the inner block within
    the same outer branch (if nothing ever does in the real file, this shape
    is moot there even though it would still be a real engine behavior).

GENERATE AT NORMAL (200), ANY PLAYER COUNT. ONE RUN - every question here is
a presence/absence at a pinned 100/0 split, not a statistical one, same shape
as RMSTEST_42's single-run read for BUG-007.

READ WITH
  python probe_scenario.py "<scenario>"
  The default object histogram is the whole reading - seven names, each
  either near its requested count or nowhere in the list.
================================================================================
*/
